  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia - World Bank Indonesia Partnership</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Australia-World Bank Indonesia Partnership (ABIP) is a five-year, AUD30 million investment that provides a platform for the majority of Australian-funded World Bank activities in Indonesia. The goal of ABIP is to support Government of Indonesia (GoI) efforts to increase inclusive economic growth, including through the promotion of gender equality. ABIP works across three priority themes: 1) Accelerating human capital development; 2) Improving economic governance and mobility; and 3) Building more and better infrastructure, with a cross-cutting focus on gender equality.</narrative>
  </description>
